  <div class="bhd-page__split-copy">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">What the review does</p>
    <h2>It revisits the scientific case for oral hydration technology</h2>
    <p>The review discusses oral rehydration physiology and the rationale for continued innovation in hydration technologies across exercise and health-related contexts. Its abstract highlights sodium and glucose cotransport across intestinal epithelia as a central mechanism supporting water uptake.</p>
    <p>Because it is a <strong>review article</strong>, it synthesizes and interprets existing literature. It is not a randomized product trial, it does not independently establish every proposed application, and it should not be cited as if it measured the clinical or performance effect of Best Hydrate itself.</p>
    <a class="bhd-page__text-link" href="https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/nutrition/articles/10.3389/fnut.2026.1851906/full" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the publisher record →</a>
